WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.321
Six levels have described a measurement system. Not one of them said what

2
00:00:05.421 --> 00:00:10.148
it is for. A gauge exists because somebody is watching a process.

3
00:00:10.233 --> 00:00:14.055
So start with what they are drawing. Subgroup means,

4
00:00:14.155 --> 00:00:17.525
and a pair of limits at three standard errors.

5
00:00:17.616 --> 00:00:21.260
These are the limits the process itself has earned -

6
00:00:21.360 --> 00:00:25.004
computed from the parts, if you could see the parts.

7
00:00:25.100 --> 00:00:29.189
But nobody sees parts. They see readings. And Level one

8
00:00:29.289 --> 00:00:33.075
settled what a reading is: the part plus the gauge,

9
00:00:33.175 --> 00:00:36.808
with the variances adding. So bring the gauge in.

10
00:00:36.900 --> 00:00:41.005
Nine percent is half a micron on this chart, which is

11
00:00:41.105 --> 00:00:45.608
why nobody has ever noticed it. Look closely at one limit.

12
00:00:47.600 --> 00:00:51.588
Every chart in every plant is drawn around a spread that

13
00:00:51.688 --> 00:00:56.116
includes its own instrument, and nothing on the chart says so.

14
00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:01.777
A wider limit is a later signal. Here is how long

15
00:01:01.877 --> 00:01:06.684
a chart waits before it notices that something real has moved.

16
00:01:06.783 --> 00:01:12.014
A three sigma shift is caught immediately whatever the gauge does, and a

17
00:01:12.114 --> 00:01:16.752
very small one is missed either way. The bill lands in between -

18
00:01:16.852 --> 00:01:21.342
which is exactly the range a chart is run to cover. Around one

19
00:01:21.442 --> 00:01:25.859
sigma the wait is thirty percent longer than it needed to be.

20
00:01:27.750 --> 00:01:30.541
Which brings the last thing, and it is

21
00:01:30.641 --> 00:01:34.193
the reason this level exists. Level four defined

22
00:01:34.293 --> 00:01:38.378
a percentage: the gauge's spread against the tolerance.

23
00:01:38.466 --> 00:01:41.102
There it is, unchanged.

24
00:01:41.200 --> 00:01:46.222
Turn it upside down. Nothing has been assumed and nothing estimated

25
00:01:46.322 --> 00:01:50.580
- this is the same statement written the other way round.

26
00:01:50.666 --> 00:01:54.509
And the left hand side is a capability index. Half a

27
00:01:54.609 --> 00:02:00.576
tolerance over three standard deviations, with the gauge's standard deviation in

28
00:02:00.676 --> 00:02:04.443
place of the process's - which is what you get when

29
00:02:04.543 --> 00:02:08.614
the process is perfect and only the instrument is left.

30
00:02:10.300 --> 00:02:15.259
Which means every published gauge gate is a capability ceiling

31
00:02:15.359 --> 00:02:19.665
that nobody prints beside it. Ten percent allows a Cpk

32
00:02:19.765 --> 00:02:23.827
of ten. Twenty allows five. Thirty - the line above

33
00:02:23.927 --> 00:02:28.152
which a gauge is rejected - allows three point three.

34
00:02:29.650 --> 00:02:34.566
One curve, and it joins the two subjects at every point along it.

35
00:02:34.650 --> 00:02:39.130
And here is where the gauge these six levels built comes out.

36
00:02:39.230 --> 00:02:44.010
Forty one percent of tolerance, so this plant cannot report a Cpk

37
00:02:44.110 --> 00:02:48.441
above two point four three - not with a better process, not

38
00:02:48.541 --> 00:02:52.646
with more parts, not ever, until the instrument changes.

39
00:02:52.733 --> 00:02:57.817
An M S A verdict was a capability verdict the whole time.

40
00:03:01.016 --> 00:03:04.789
One last thing the chart is not able to do. The spread

41
00:03:04.889 --> 00:03:09.308
it estimates inside a subgroup is made of two things: the parts

42
00:03:09.408 --> 00:03:13.540
differing from each other, and the gauge failing to repeat.

43
00:03:13.633 --> 00:03:16.557
Here is that spread, all of it parts.

44
00:03:16.650 --> 00:03:20.427
Now hand some of it to the gauge. Watch the number the

45
00:03:20.527 --> 00:03:24.879
chart reports. It does not move - it cannot, because the chart

46
00:03:24.979 --> 00:03:29.690
only ever saw the total. And underneath, the true capability of the

47
00:03:29.790 --> 00:03:34.070
process runs from one point oh four to two point three three.

48
00:03:34.166 --> 00:03:38.462
A capable process with a poor gauge and a poor process with

49
00:03:38.562 --> 00:03:43.752
a perfect one look identical from here. No amount of charting separates

50
00:03:43.852 --> 00:03:47.775
them, which is why a gauge study is a separate study -

51
00:03:47.875 --> 00:03:51.202
and why this site exists beside the other one.

52
00:03:53.200 --> 00:03:57.749
Seven levels. A gauge is a process and it has variation. Two

53
00:03:57.849 --> 00:04:03.019
questions hiding in one word. The term average and range cannot see.

54
00:04:03.119 --> 00:04:07.823
A percentage, and what it is a percentage of. Precision is not

55
00:04:07.923 --> 00:04:12.396
accuracy. The gauge that says pass. And the handshake back.

56
00:04:13.983 --> 00:04:19.378
Every number in these seven levels was computed when the page was built, by

57
00:04:19.478 --> 00:04:24.507
the same library the tests read. None of it is asserted. And the chart

58
00:04:24.607 --> 00:04:29.123
that consumes all of it is on the other site, where it belongs.

